cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this tutorial or its notebooks, please cite it as below."
title: "From Haar Random States to Quantum Machine Learning: A Hands-On Numerical Tutorial"
abstract: >-
  A self-contained, runnable tutorial on randomness, scrambling, and learning in
  quantum systems. It builds the Haar/Weingarten averaging toolkit and follows it
  across random matrix theory, scrambling dynamics, unitary designs, classical
  shadows, randomized benchmarking, the Hayden-Preskill protocol, and barren
  plateaus in quantum machine learning, with 41 executable Jupyter notebooks and
  a complete set of worked exercises.
type: software
